Fly's direction and landing: the flight is mirrored when the destination
lies east (Port_FlyEast, asked as the flight out begins): the Pokemon
leaves ball, swoops and returns on the right, its rider faces and mounts
east, the follower sprite plays its east-facing frames (its own seat), the
bird's affine turns go the other way. On the new map the Pokemon no longer
waits for the camera to settle: it comes in beside the camera coming down
(Port_FlyLanding, 0..255 of the way) and reaches the player as it settles,
the rider let go on its angle rather than a timer. Port_FlyBusy now only
holds the landing while inside the cloud.
Applies after 0084-fly-on-the-pokemon.patch; apply with tools/bootstrap.py.

